    "long_instructions": "> Toni got an email from their coach.<br>\r\n> The email is about practice next week.<br>\r\n> Toni is not sure how to respond.<br>\r\n> He decides to ask an AI for help.<br>\r\n\r\n**Step 1: Write Toni’s First Message**\r\n1. Write a short message as if you are Toni asking the AI for help.\r\n\r\n\tYour message should:\r\nBe 1–2 sentences\r\nInclude no real names or personal information\r\nDescribe the situation in a simple way\r\n\r\nTry this:\r\n“I got an email from my coach about practice.”\r\n\r\n\r\n**Step 2: Add One Emotion Word**\r\n1. Copy your message.\r\n2. Change only one word by adding an emotion word. Everything else stays the same.\r\n\tExamples:  great, excited, angry, upset\r\n\r\n**Step 3: Compare the AI’s Responses**\r\nRead both responses from the AI.\r\n\r\n*Ask yourself:*\r\n- How did the tone change?\r\n- Did the AI sound more serious or more calm?\r\n- Which emotion do you think the AI reacted to?"
  },
